fair share = 913/8 = 114.125
heavy-task excess = 120 - 114.125 = 5.875 columns = 4.896% of 120
band bound on the projection leaves = 4.896% * 2461.180 ms = 120.5 ms (upper bound: the
  leaves also contain SwiGLU, the k = 1 pass, and fixed dispatch overhead/wait; a perfectly
  balanced integer 7 x 114 + 115 split leaves 115 as the longest band, so the saving is
  (120 - 115)/120 * 2461.180 = 102.55 ms; the 0.875-column excess over 114.125 is unavoidable)
tail unused share = (120 - 73)/120 = 39.17%
