participant  cycles G  instr G  IPC   task s  GHz    off-CPU vs caller s
caller       18.302    42.351   2.31  5.0146  3.650  0
worker 1     16.340    40.393   2.47  4.4702  3.655  0.544
worker 2     16.306    39.810   2.44  4.4669  3.650  0.548
worker 3     16.261    39.829   2.45  4.4507  3.654  0.564
worker 4     16.263    39.806   2.45  4.4503  3.654  0.564
worker 5     16.296    39.802   2.44  4.4619  3.652  0.553
worker 6     16.279    39.813   2.45  4.4618  3.648  0.553
tail         15.793    30.972   1.96  4.3253  3.651  0.689
total       131.840   312.776   2.37

# cycles/task-clock = 3.648-3.655 GHz on all eight. The caller's excess over the six-worker mean
# is 18.302 - 16.291 = 2.011 G; /3.651 GHz = 0.551 s; the six off-CPU is 5.0146 - 4.4603 = 0.554 s.
# The tail excess 18.302 - 15.793 = 2.509 G; /3.651 = 0.687 s; off-CPU 5.0146 - 4.3253 = 0.689 s.
# At a uniform clock, cycles = clock * on-CPU seconds, so a spinning worker accrues cycles at the
# caller's rate and caller-serial wall cancels in the difference. The cycle excess is the workers'
# off-CPU time by construction; it cannot price serial glue.

